#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:24
msgid ""
"These are in-progress notes for the upcoming Clang {{env.config.version}} "
"release. Release notes for previous releases can be found on [the Releases "
"Page](https://llvm.org/releases/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:30
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "簡介"

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:32
msgid ""
"This document contains the release notes for the Clang C/C++/Objective-C "
"frontend, part of the LLVM Compiler Infrastructure, release {{env.config."
"release}}. Here we describe the status of Clang in some detail, including "
"major improvements from the previous release and new feature work. For the "
"general LLVM release notes, see [the LLVM documentation](https://llvm.org/"
"docs/ReleaseNotes.html). For the libc++ release notes, see [this page]"
"(https://libcxx.llvm.org/ReleaseNotes.html). All LLVM releases may be "
"downloaded from the [LLVM releases web site](https://llvm.org/releases/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:41
msgid ""
"For more information about Clang or LLVM, including information about the "
"latest release, please see the [Clang Web Site](https://clang.llvm.org) or "
"the [LLVM Web Site](https://llvm.org)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:45
msgid "Potentially Breaking Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:47
msgid "C/C++ Language Potentially Breaking Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:49
msgid ""
"Clang now makes it ill-formed to try to `break` out of or `continue` a loop "
"inside its own condition, increment, or init-statement in all C and C++ "
"language modes. This means that code such as"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:56
msgid ""
"is now ill-formed. An outer loop can still be broken out of or continued so "
"long as the inner loop is in the body of the outer loop:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:69
msgid "This also resolves a divergence from GCC: in a construct such as"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:77
msgid ""
"Clang would previously `break` out of the `while` loop, whereas GCC (since "
"version 9) would `break` out of the `for` loop here. Now, Clang and GCC both "
"break out of the `for` loop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:80
msgid ""
"Clang now parses line and digit directives, module names, and original "
"filenames as unevaluated strings. This means that code containing strings "
"with escape sequences such as"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:89
msgid "are now ill-formed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:91
msgid ""
"`__has_feature(modules)` is no longer true when just `-std=c++20` (or "
"higher) is passed. It's only true if `-fmodules` is passed, which enables "
"Clang's module map semantics. Objective-C++ of the form"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:103
msgid ""
"previously took the `@import` branch under `-std=c++20` even though no "
"module maps were in use, which would always fail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:106
msgid ""
"`__cpp_modules` continues to be the standard macro to use to check if C++20 "
"modules are available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:109
msgid "C++ Specific Potentially Breaking Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:111
msgid ""
"Clang now more aggressively optimizes away stores to objects after they are "
"dead. This behavior can be disabled with `-fno-lifetime-dse`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:113
msgid ""
"Clang now correctly rejects `export` declarations in module implementation "
"partitions. (#GH107602)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:115
msgid ""
"Template argument deduction now treats the `N` in `_BitInt(N)` as being of "
"type `std::size_t` instead of `int`, matching the deduction of array sizes "
"from `int(&)[N]`. This is a breaking change for code that depended on the "
"previously deduced type. (#GH195033)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:119
msgid ""
"Clang now rejects nested local classes defined in a different block scope "
"than their parent class. (#GH193472)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:122
msgid "ABI Changes in This Version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:124
msgid ""
"Fixed incorrect struct layout for `_BitInt` bitfields wider than 255 bits on "
"MSVC targets. Internal bitfield tracking fields were changed from `unsigned "
"char` to `uint64_t` to prevent overflow. This might be an ABI break for such "
"structs compared to earlier Clang versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:128
msgid ""
"Fixed a number of issues with the `__regcall` calling convention for passing "
"structs on non-Windows x86-64 targets, including a crash when handling empty "
"struct arguments. This changes how structs that contain arrays, floating "
"point types, or `_Complex float` types are passed, and may introduce "
"incompatibilities with code compiled by earlier versions of Clang that uses "
"the `__regcall` calling convention on these targets. (#GH62999) (#GH98635)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:134
msgid ""
"Fixed Itanium mangling for lambdas in instantiated non-static data member "
"initializers by preserving the field-name closure-prefix. This changes the "
"mangled names for affected lambdas. (#GH190555)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:137
msgid ""
"Clang now uses MSVC-compatible manglings for supported AArch64 SVE builtin "
"types when targeting the Microsoft ABI. This changes symbol names for "
"affected declarations compared to previous Clang releases. (#GH196170)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:140
msgid ""
"The resume and destroy functions of C++20 coroutines now use the platform C "
"calling convention instead of LLVM's internal `fastcc`. This makes the "
"coroutine ABI stable across LLVM versions and interoperable with other "
"compilers. On most targets this is not a breaking change because `fastcc` "
"and the platform C calling convention agree for `void(ptr)`. It is an ABI "
"break on i686, MIPS O32, PowerPC64 ELFv1, and Lanai."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:146
msgid ""
"`va_arg` on clang aarch64 msvc now reads types with 16-byte size and "
"alignment (e.g. `__int128`) with their actual alignment (instead of an "
"alignment of 8 which was used before). Such c-variadic arguments are already "
"passed as aligned, so previously reading the argument could read padding. "
"Clang now matches how MSVC reads such c-variadic arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:151
msgid ""
"Fixed incorrect struct return when single large vector (256/512-bit) used on "
"x86-64 targets. (#GH203760) The bug was introduced since Clang 21. "
"(#GH120670)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:153
msgid ""
"Clang now applies MSVC's MD5 shortening to over-long Microsoft C++ RTTI type "
"descriptor name strings, matching the behavior already used for the RTTI "
"symbol names. Previously the full name string was always emitted, so deeply "
"nested template types (for example, ones containing local lambdas) could "
"produce very large writable `.data` sections. Emitted RTTI name strings "
"change only for types whose name exceeds the length limit. (#GH206313)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:159
msgid ""
"Fixed Itanium mangling for lambdas in default member initializers of local "
"classes to use `<local-name>` encoding, preventing mangling collisions "
"between distinct local classes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:163
msgid "AST Dumping Potentially Breaking Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:165
msgid ""
"The JSON AST dump now includes all fields from `AvailabilityAttr`: "
"`platform`, `introduced`, `deprecated`, `obsoleted`, `unavailable`, "
"`message`, `strict`, `replacement`, `priority`, and `environment`. "
"Previously, these fields were missing from the JSON output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:169
msgid ""
"Colons that appear at the end of a ParamCommentCommand name are not "
"serialized as part of the name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:171
msgid ""
"AST pretty-printing now respects `PrintingPolicy::FullyQualifiedName` when "
"printing `DeclRefExpr` names, including expression-form non-type template "
"arguments in printed types. Previously, these references could be printed "
"unqualified. (#GH206041)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:176
msgid "Clang Frontend Potentially Breaking Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:178
msgid ""
"HIPSPV toolchain: `--offload-targets=spirv{32,64}` option is deprecated and "
"will be removed when the new offload driver becomes default. The replacement "
"for the option is `--offload-targets=spirv{32,64}-unknown-chipstar` when "
"using the new offload driver (`--offload-new-driver`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:183
msgid ""
"The new driver (`--offload-new-driver`) is now default for all offloading "
"compilations. This changes the ABI for relocatable device code. Currently, "
"libraries will need to be recompiled, or used with (`--no-offload-new-"
"driver`). This option will be removed in the next release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:187
msgid ""
"Clang no longer defines the `__cpp_impl_coroutine` feature test macro under "
"the 32-bit x86 Microsoft ABI, as support for coroutines on this target is "
"incomplete. When using coroutines on this target a warning is emmitted to "
"indicate the lack of full support. That warning can be disabled with `-Wno-"
"coroutines-unsupported-target`. (see #GH59382)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:192
msgid "Clang Python Bindings Potentially Breaking Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:194
msgid ""
"Remove `CompletionString.Availability`. No libclang interfaces returned "
"instances of it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:196
msgid ""
"`CompletionString.availability` now returns instances of `CompletionString."
"AvailabilityKindCompat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:198
msgid ""
"Instances of `AvailabilityKindCompat` have the same `__str__` representation "
"as the previous `CompletionChunk.Kind` and are equality-comparable with the "
"existing `AvailabilityKind` enum. It will be replaced by `AvailabilityKind` "
"in a future release. When this happens, the return type of `CompletionString."
"availability` will change to `AvailabilityKind`, so it is recommended to use "
"`AvailabilityKind` to compare with the return values of `CompletionString."
"availability`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:205
msgid ""
"Remove `availabilityKinds`. In this release, uses of `availabilityKinds` "
"need to be replaced by `CompletionString.AvailabilityKind`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:208
msgid "`CompletionChunk.kind` now returns instances of `CompletionChunkKind`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:210
msgid ""
"Instances of `CompletionChunkKind` have the same `__str__` representation as "
"the previous `CompletionChunk.Kind` for compatibility. These representations "
"will be changed in a future release to match other enums."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:214
msgid ""
"Remove `completionChunkKindMap`. In this release, uses of "
"`completionChunkKindMap` need to be replaced by `CompletionChunkKind`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:217
msgid ""
"Move `SPELLING_CACHE` into `CompletionChunk` and change it to use "
"`CompletionChunkKind` instances as keys, instead of the enum values. An "
"alias is kept in the form of a `SPELLING_CACHE` variable, but it only "
"supports `__getitem__` and `__contains__`. It will be removed in a future "
"release. Please migrate to using `CompletionChunk.SPELLING_CACHE` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:223
msgid ""
"`SourceLocation` and `SourceRange` now use `NotImplemented` to delegate "
"equality checks (`__eq__`) to the other object they are compared with when "
"they are of different classes. They previously returned `False` when "
"compared with objects of other classes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:228
msgid ""
"`TranslationUnit.get_tokens` now throws an error if both the `extent` and "
"`locations` argument are passed. Previousy, `locations` took precedence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:231
msgid ""
"`_CXUnsavedFile` will be renamed to `UnsavedFile` for consistency. "
"`UnsavedFile` is already available to use and existing uses should be "
"adapted to refer to it instead. `_CXUnsavedFile` will be removed in a future "
"release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:236
msgid "OpenCL Potentially Breaking Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:238
msgid ""
"Clang now diagnoses zero-length arrays as errors in OpenCL. OpenCL C 3.0 "
"section 6.11.d states that \"Variable length arrays and structures with "
"flexible (or unsized) arrays are not supported.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:243
msgid "What's New in Clang {{env.config.release}}?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:245
msgid "C++ Language Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:247
msgid ""
"`__is_trivially_equality_comparable` no longer returns false for all enum "
"types. (#GH132672)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:248
msgid ""
"`auto` parameters are now available in all C++ language modes as an "
"extension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:250
msgid "C++2d Feature Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:252
msgid ""
"Added compiler flags `-std=c++2d` and `-std=gnu++2d` for experimental C++2d "
"implementation work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:254
msgid ""
"Clang now supports [P3733R1](https://wg21.link/p3733r1>) More named "
"universal character escapes. The change is applied as a DR to all C++ "
"language modes. (#GH203944)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:257
msgid "C++2c Feature Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:259
msgid ""
"Clang now propagates `constinit` and `constexpr` in structured bindings with "
"tuple-like initializers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:261
msgid "C++23 Feature Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:263
msgid ""
"Partially implement Itanium mangling for pack indexing. Partially "
"substituted packs are not yet supported. (#GH112003)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:265
msgid "C++20 Feature Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:267
msgid ""
"Clang now supports [P1857R3](https://wg21.link/p1857r3) Modules Dependency "
"Discovery. (#GH54047)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:269
msgid "C++17 Feature Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:271
msgid "Resolutions to C++ Defect Reports"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:273
msgid ""
"Implemented [CWG1780 Explicit instantiation/specialization of generic lambda "
"operator()](https://cplusplus.github.io/CWG/issues/1780.html)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:275
msgid ""
"Clang now allows omitting `typename` before a template name in a conversion "
"operator, implementing [CWG2413](https://wg21.link/cwg2413)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:277
msgid ""
"Member specializations can now be declared in class scope, according to the "
"resolution of [CWG727](https://wg21.link/cwg727). This is still not "
"sufficient to resolve that core issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:280
msgid ""
"Clang now uses non-reference types for structured bindings whose initializer "
"returns a prvalue. This resolves [CWG3135](https://wg21.link/cwg3135)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:283
msgid "C Language Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:285
msgid "C2y Feature Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:287
msgid ""
"Implemented the type-specific C2y `<stdbit.h>` rotate functions with "
"constexpr evaluation support: `stdc_rotate_left_{uc,us,ui,ul,ull}` and "
"`stdc_rotate_right_{uc,us,ui,ul,ull}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:291
msgid ""
"Implemented C2y `<stdbit.h>` memory reversal functions: "
"`__builtin_stdc_memreverse8` / `stdc_memreverse8` (in-place byte reversal of "
"a byte array) and `stdc_memreverse8u{8,16,32,64}` (byte-swap of an exact-"
"width unsigned integer value, usable in constant expressions)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:296
msgid "C23 Feature Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:298
msgid ""
"Clang now allows C23 `constexpr` struct member access through the dot "
"operator in constant expressions. (#GH178349)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:299
msgid ""
"Fixed a failing assertion when validating an invalid structure redefinition "
"with a member which uses an incomplete enumeration type. (#GH190227)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:301
msgid "Clang now supports the C23 `wN` and `wfN` length modifiers. (#GH116962)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:302
msgid ""
"Clang now recognizes the C23 `H`, `D`, and `DD` length modifiers in format "
"strings and diagnoses their use because Clang does not yet support the "
"corresponding decimal floating-point types, `_Decimal32`, `_Decimal64`, and "
"`_Decimal128`. (#GH116962)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:305
msgid ""
"Fixed a bug with deducing qualified inferred types with `auto`. `auto` can "
"now be combined with `restrict` or `_Atomic` to form a properly-qualified "
"type. (#GH207466)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:309
msgid "Objective-C Language Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:311
msgid ""
"Clang now emits Objective-C number, array, and dictionary literals as "
"compile-time constant data structures rather than runtime `objc_msgSend` "
"calls on targets whose runtime supports constant literal classes. The "
"feature can be disabled altogether with `-fno-objc-constant-literals`, or "
"selectively per literal kind with `-fno-constant-nsnumber-literals`, `-fno-"
"constant-nsarray-literals`, and `-fno-constant-nsdictionary-literals`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:319
msgid "Non-comprehensive list of changes in this release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:321
msgid ""
"Added support for floating point and pointer values in most `__atomic_` "
"builtins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:323
msgid ""
"Added `__builtin_stdc_rotate_left` and `__builtin_stdc_rotate_right` for bit "
"rotation of unsigned integers including `_BitInt` types. Rotation counts are "
"normalized modulo the bit-width and support negative values. Usable in "
"constant expressions. Implicit conversion is supported for class/struct "
"types with conversion operators."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:328
msgid ""
"Implemented the following C23 `<stdbit.h>` builtins with `_BitInt` support "
"and constexpr evaluation: `__builtin_stdc_leading_zeros`, "
"`__builtin_stdc_leading_ones`, `__builtin_stdc_trailing_zeros`, "
"`__builtin_stdc_trailing_ones`, `__builtin_stdc_first_leading_zero`, "
"`__builtin_stdc_first_leading_one`, `__builtin_stdc_first_trailing_zero`, "
"`__builtin_stdc_first_trailing_one`, `__builtin_stdc_count_zeros`, "
"`__builtin_stdc_count_ones`, `__builtin_stdc_has_single_bit`, "
"`__builtin_stdc_bit_width`, `__builtin_stdc_bit_floor`, and "
"`__builtin_stdc_bit_ceil`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:337
msgid ""
"Implemented the type-specific C23 `<stdbit.h>` functions with constexpr "
"evaluation support: `stdc_leading_zeros_{uc,us,ui,ul,ull}`, "
"`stdc_leading_ones_{uc,us,ui,ul,ull}`, `stdc_trailing_zeros_{uc,us,ui,ul,ull}"
"`, `stdc_trailing_ones_{uc,us,ui,ul,ull}`, `stdc_first_leading_zero_{uc,us,"
"ui,ul,ull}`, `stdc_first_leading_one_{uc,us,ui,ul,ull}`, "
"`stdc_first_trailing_zero_{uc,us,ui,ul,ull}`, `stdc_first_trailing_one_{uc,"
"us,ui,ul,ull}`, `stdc_count_zeros_{uc,us,ui,ul,ull}`, `stdc_count_ones_{uc,"
"us,ui,ul,ull}`, `stdc_has_single_bit_{uc,us,ui,ul,ull}`, `stdc_bit_width_{uc,"
"us,ui,ul,ull}`, `stdc_bit_floor_{uc,us,ui,ul,ull}`, and `stdc_bit_ceil_{uc,"
"us,ui,ul,ull}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:353
msgid ""
"A new generic bit-reverse builtin function `__builtin_bitreverseg` that "
"extends bit-reversal support to all standard integers type, including "
"`_BitInt`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:356
msgid ""
"Added `__builtin_elementwise_clmul` for carry-less multiplication of "
"integers including `_BitInt` types. This includes constexpr evaluation "
"support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:359
msgid ""
"Added `__builtin_elementwise_pext` and `__builtin_elementwise_pdep` for "
"parallel bit extract and parallel bit deposit operations on integers "
"including `_BitInt` types. This includes constexpr evaluation support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:362
msgid ""
"Deprecated float types support from `__builtin_elementwise_max` and "
"`__builtin_elementwise_min`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:364
msgid ""
"Added header `endian.h` which contains byte order helpers specified in POSIX"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:365
msgid "Added #pragma loop licm(disable) for llvm.loop.licm.disable metadata"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:366
msgid ""
"Added a new `ExplicitInstantiationDecl` AST node to represent explicit "
"template instantiations (e.g., `template void foo<int>();` or `extern "
"template class S<int>;`). Previously, source location information for "
"explicit instantiation statements was discarded after parsing. The new node "
"preserves the full source range including the `extern` and `template` "
"keywords, qualifiers, template arguments as written, and the declared type, "
"enabling tools such as language servers and refactoring engines to "
"accurately map source locations back to explicit instantiation sites."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:374
msgid ""
"`typeid` on references and pointers of `final` types no longer emits a "
"vtable lookup at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:376
msgid "Updated support for Unicode from 15.1 to 18.0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:377
msgid ""
"Linux and Windows toolchains now support Clang multilibs using `-fmultilib-"
"flag=`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:379
msgid ""
"The SafeStack builtins `__builtin___get_unsafe_stack_ptr`, "
"`__builtin___get_unsafe_stack_bottom`, `__builtin___get_unsafe_stack_top`, "
"and `__builtin___get_unsafe_stack_start` are now deprecated. Use the "
"corresponding functions from `<sanitizer/safestack_interface.h>` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:384
msgid "New Compiler Flags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:386
msgid ""
"New option `-fms-anonymous-structs` / `-fno-ms-anonymous-structs` added to "
"enable or disable Microsoft's anonymous struct/union extension without "
"enabling other `-fms-extensions` features (#GH177607)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:389
msgid ""
"New option `--precompile-reduced-bmi` allows build system to generate a "
"reduced BMI only for a C++20 importable module unit. Previously the users "
"can only generate the reduced BMI as a by-product, e.g, an object files or a "
"full BMI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:393
msgid ""
"New `-cc1` option `-fexperimental-overflow-behavior-types` added to enable "
"parsing of the experimental `overflow_behavior` type attribute and type "
"specifiers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:396
msgid ""
"New `-cl` option `/d2guardnochecks` added to match MSVC. When Windows "
"Control Flow Guard (CFG) is enabled by other options, it will instruct Clang "
"to emit the CFG metadata, but disable adding checks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:399
msgid ""
"New option `-fdiagnostics-show-inlining-chain` added to show inlining chain "
"notes for `[[gnu::warning]]` and `[[gnu::error]]` diagnostics. When a "
"function with these attributes is called from an inlined context, Clang can "
"now show which functions were inlined to reach the call. When debug info is "
"available (`-gline-directives-only` (implicitly enabled at `-g1`) or "
"higher), accurate source locations are used; otherwise, a heuristic fallback "
"is used with a note suggesting how to enable debug info for better accuracy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:406
msgid ""
"New option `-fwin-cfg-mechanism=` added to control the mechanism used by "
"Control Flow Guard on Windows. Accepted values are `automatic` (default), "
"`dispatch`, and `check`. The `dispatch` mechanism uses the dispatch function "
"to perform indirect call checks and can improve performance, while `check` "
"uses the traditional check mechanism."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:411
msgid ""
"New `-cl` option `/d2guardcfgdispatch` added to match MSVC. This acts as a "
"shorthand for `-fwin-cfg-mechanism=dispatch`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:413
msgid ""
"New `-cl` option `/d2guardcfgdispatch-` added to match MSVC. This acts as a "
"shorthand for `-fwin-cfg-mechanism=check`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:415
msgid ""
"New option `-f[no-]strict-bool` added to control whether Clang can assume "
"that `bool` values loaded from memory cannot have a bit pattern other than 0 "
"or 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:418
msgid ""
"New option `-fcrash-diagnostics-tar` added to create an archive of crash "
"reproducer files for easier bug filing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:420
msgid ""
"There are a new pair of flags for riscv32 called `-mzilsd-word-align` and `-"
"mzilsd-strict-align` which control whether Zilsd accesses are allowed to be "
"aligned to 4-byte alignment rather than fully unaligned or fully (8-byte) "
"aligned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:424
msgid ""
"New `-cl` option `/pathmap:` added to match MSVC. This option acts as a "
"clang's `-ffile-prefix-map=value` and has known differences in behaviour "
"with the CL's option that do not affect the functionality: nomalizes the "
"macro prefix map pathes -- removes `./` and uses the target's platform- "
"specific path separator character when expanding the preprocessor macros -- "
"`-ffile-reproducible` (but not the debug and coverage prefix maps); does not "
"require `/experimental:deterministic` as by MSVC. It needed for removing a "
"hostname from a mangling hash gen, but clang-cl does not use a hostname when "
"generates the hashes. Known issues -- does not remap the source file pathes "
"within PCH/PCM files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:434
msgid ""
"New `-cl` option `/experimental:deterministic` added to match CL's option. "
"This enables warning emission on usage of non-deterministic macros "
"`__DATE__`, `__TIME__` and `__TIMESTAMP__` and provides reproducable COFF's "
"timestamp for the output object files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:438
msgid ""
"New `-cl` option `/d1nodatetime` added to match CL's option. This option "
"undefines the standard macros `__DATE__`, `__TIME__` and `__TIMESTAMP__` to "
"allow reproducable builds. These macros can be redefined from the command "
"line if necessary. `/d1nodatetime-` can be used to turn this feature off if "
"necessary to override the common build settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:444
msgid "Deprecated Compiler Flags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:446
msgid "Modified Compiler Flags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:448
msgid ""
"The `-mno-outline` and `-moutline` compiler flags are now allowed on RISC-V "
"and X86, which both support the machine outliner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:449
msgid ""
"The `-mno-outline` flag will now add the `nooutline` IR attribute, so that `-"
"mno-outline` and `-moutline` objects can be mixed correctly during LTO."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:451
msgid ""
"The `-fzero-call-used-regs` compiler flag is now allowed on RISC-V, only the "
"\"skip\", \"used-gpr\", \"used-gpr-arg\", \"all-gpr\" and \"all-gpr-arg\" "
"options are supported for the moment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:454
msgid ""
"Slightly changed hash id generation to get the unique linkage symbols names "
"by `-unique-internal-linkage-names` option. Now it uses a path that "
"normalized in favor of the target system (same as the preprocessor does for "
"the file macros) and allows the reproducable IDs on any build system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:458
msgid ""
"`-fprofile-update=atomic` will now promote counter updates out of loops, "
"similar to the non-atomic case ([#202487](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-"
"project/pull/202487))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:460
msgid ""
"The `-cl` `/Brepro` option was modified to match the original CL's option "
"and now defines the standard macros `__DATE__`, `__TIME__` and "
"`__TIMESTAMP__` to \"1\". The previous functionality remains unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:463
msgid ""
"The `-fms-kernel` flag will now implicitly add `-fno-delete-null-pointer-"
"checks`. Still `-fdelete-null-pointer-checks` can be used to override this "
"behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:466
msgid "Removed Compiler Flags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:468
msgid "Attribute Changes in Clang"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:470
msgid ""
"Added new attribute `stack_protector_ignore` to opt specific local variables "
"out of the analysis which determines if a function should get a stack "
"protector. A function will still generate a stack protector if other local "
"variables or command line flags require it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:475
msgid ""
"Added a new attribute, `[[clang::no_outline]]` to suppress outlining from "
"annotated functions. This uses the LLVM `nooutline` attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:478
msgid ""
"Introduced a new type attribute `__attribute__((overflow_behavior))` which "
"currently accepts either `wrap` or `trap` as an argument, enabling type-"
"level control over overflow behavior. There is also an accompanying type "
"specifier for each behavior kind via `__ob_wrap` and `__ob_trap`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:483
msgid ""
"Introduced a new function attribute `__attribute__((__personality__(...)))` "
"to explicitly specify the personality routine for exception handling. THis "
"is meant to be a low level tool for language runtime authors to associate a "
"foreign language personality with a given function. Note that this does not "
"perform any ABI validation for the personality routine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:489
msgid ""
"{doc}`ThreadSafetyAnalysis` attributes now correctly handle implicit member "
"accesses in C, and parameter attributes in C++. This improves diagnostic "
"precision and fixes false positives."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:493
msgid ""
"The {doc}`ThreadSafetyAnalysis` attributes `guarded_by` and `pt_guarded_by` "
"now accept multiple capability arguments with refined access semantics: "
"*writing* requires all listed capabilities to be held exclusively, while "
"*reading* requires at least one to be held. This is sound because any writer "
"must hold all capabilities, so holding any one prevents concurrent writes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:500
msgid ""
"{doc}`ThreadSafetyAnalysis` attributes like `acquire_capability`, "
"`release_capability`, `requires_capability`, `locks_excluded`, "
"`try_acquire_capability`, and `assert_capability` can now be applied to "
"function pointer variables and fields. The analysis checks calls through "
"annotated function pointers the same way it checks direct function calls. "
"Only plain function pointers are supported; pointers-to-member functions, "
"blocks, or wrappers (e.g. `std::function`) are not yet supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:508
msgid ""
"The `[[clang::unsafe_buffer_usage]]` attribute is now supported in API "
"notes. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:517
msgid ""
"When using `-Wunsafe-buffer-usage` without `-fsafe-buffer-usage-"
"suggestions`, warnings are now emitted only once per source file. Pre-"
"compiled code (such as PCH or module headers) is no longer repeatedly "
"analyzed, as it is analyzed during its initial compilation. (Traditionally "
"included headers are still analyzed within each translation unit that "
"includes them). This behavior matches most of other `-W` diagnostics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:525
msgid ""
"When `-fsafe-buffer-usage-suggestions` is enabled, the behavior remains the "
"same as before: pre-compiled code is deserialized and analyzed alongside the "
"translation unit that uses it, because fix-it suggestion analysis requires "
"full visibility of the translation unit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:531
msgid ""
"Added support for `[[msvc::forceinline]]` for functions and `[[msvc::"
"forceinline_calls]]` for statements. Both are aliases to `[[clang::"
"always_inline]]` with additional checks to ensure that they are only "
"accepted in places where MSVC also does."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:536
msgid ""
"The AMDGPU `amdgpu_num_sgpr` and `amdgpu_num_vgpr` attributes are now "
"deprecated. Clang emits a `-Wdeprecated-declarations` warning when they are "
"used. Use `amdgpu_waves_per_eu` instead to control SGPR and VGPR usage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:541
msgid ""
"Clang now allows GNU attributes between a member declarator and bit-field "
"width. (#GH184954)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:543
msgid ""
"The `[[clang::noescape]]` attribute now disallows deallocating memory "
"through the annotated parameter. This information is currently not exposed "
"to LLVM for optimization purposes, to prevent breaking existing adopters. It "
"may instead be used by warnings and static analyses to provide more "
"information about pointer lifetimes. It may be used to power optimizations "
"in the future, however there are no concrete plans to do so at the moment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:550
msgid ""
"The attributes `[[clang::opencl_global_device]]` and `[[clang::"
"opencl_global_host]]` are now deprecated. Clang emits a `-Wdeprecated-"
"attributes` warning when they are used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:554
msgid ""
"The `modular_format` attribute now supports the `fixed` aspect for C ISO "
"18037 fixed-point `printf` specifiers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:557
msgid ""
"The `const` and `pure` attributes only apply to functions; they are now "
"diagnosed and ignored when applied to anything else."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:560
msgid "Improvements to Clang's diagnostics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:562
msgid ""
"Fixed bug in `-Wdocumentation` so that it correctly handles explicit "
"function template instantiations (#64087)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:565
msgid ""
"Fixed concept template parameters not being recognized in `-Wdocumentation` "
"when mentioned in tparam comments. (#GH64087)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:568
msgid ""
"`-Wunused-but-set-variable` now diagnoses file-scope variables with internal "
"linkage (`static` storage class) that are assigned but never used. This new "
"coverage is added under the subgroup `-Wunused-but-set-global`, allowing it "
"to be disabled independently with `-Wno-unused-but-set-global`. (#GH148361)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:574
msgid ""
"`-Wunused-template` is now part of `-Wunused` (which is enabled by `-Wall`). "
"It diagnoses unused function and variable templates with internal linkage, "
"which in a header is a latent ODR hazard. It can be disabled with `-Wno-"
"unused-template`. (#GH202945)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:579
msgid ""
"Added `-Wlifetime-safety` to enable lifetime safety analysis, a CFG-based "
"intra-procedural analysis that detects use-after-free and related temporal "
"safety bugs. See the [RFC](https://discourse.llvm.org/t/rfc-intra-procedural-"
"lifetime-analysis-in-clang/86291) for more details. By design, this warning "
"is enabled in `-Weverything`. To disable the analysis, use `-Wno-lifetime-"
"safety` or `-fno-lifetime-safety`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:586
msgid ""
"Added `-Wlifetime-safety-suggestions` to enable lifetime annotation "
"suggestions. This provides suggestions for function parameters that should "
"be marked `[[clang::lifetimebound]]` based on lifetime analysis. For "
"example, for the following function:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:595
msgid "Clang will suggest:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:607
msgid ""
"Added `-Wlifetime-safety-noescape` to detect misuse of `[[clang::noescape]]` "
"annotation where the parameter escapes through return. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:614
msgid "Clang will warn:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:625
msgid ""
"Added `-Wlifetime-safety-dangling-field` to detect dangling field references "
"when stack memory escapes to class fields. This is part of `-Wlifetime-"
"safety` and detects cases where local variables or parameters are stored in "
"fields but outlive their scope. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:637
msgid ""
"Improved `-Wassign-enum` performance by caching enum enumerator values. "
"(#GH176454)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:639
msgid ""
"Clang now emits `-Wpsabi` diagnostics for externally visible x86-64 function "
"definitions that return or take AVX or AVX-512 vector types without enabling "
"the corresponding target feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:643
msgid ""
"Fixed a false negative in `-Warray-bounds` where the warning was suppressed "
"when accessing a member function on a past-the-end array element. (#GH179128)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:647
msgid ""
"Added a missing space to the FixIt for the `implicit-int` group of "
"diagnostics and made sure that only one such diagnostic and FixIt is emitted "
"per declaration group. (#GH179354)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:650
msgid ""
"Fixed the Fix-It insertion point for `expected ';' after alias declaration` "
"when parsing alias declarations involving a token-split `>>` sequence (for "
"example, `using A = X<int>>;`). (#GH184425)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:654
msgid ""
"Fixed incorrect `implicitly deleted` diagnostic for explicitly deleted "
"candidate function. (#GH185693)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:657
msgid ""
"The `-Wloop-analysis` warning has been extended to catch more cases of "
"variable modification inside lambda expressions (#GH132038)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:660
msgid ""
"Clang now emits `-Wsizeof-pointer-memaccess` when snprintf/vsnprintf use the "
"sizeof the destination buffer(dynamically allocated) in the len "
"parameter(#GH162366)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:663
msgid ""
"Added `-Wmodule-map-path-outside-directory` (off by default) to warn on "
"header and umbrella directory paths that use `..` to refer outside the "
"module directory in module maps found via implicit search (`-fimplicit-"
"module-maps`). This does not affect module maps specified explicitly via `-"
"fmodule-map-file=`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:669
msgid ""
"Honour `[[maybe_unused]]` attribute on private fields. `-Wunused-private-"
"field` no longer emits a warning for annotated private fields."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:673
msgid ""
"Improved `-Wgnu-zero-variadic-macro-arguments` to suggest using `__VA_OPT__` "
"if the current language version supports it(#GH188624)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:676
msgid ""
"Clang now emits an error when implicitly casting a complex type to a built-"
"in vector type. (#GH186805)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:678
msgid ""
"Added `-Wnonportable-include-path-separator` (off by default) to catch "
"#include directives that use backslashes as a path separator. The warning "
"includes a FixIt to change all the backslashes to forward slashes, so that "
"the code can automatically be made portable to other host platforms that "
"don't support backslashes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:684
msgid ""
"Clang now explains why template deduction fails for explicit template "
"arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:686
msgid ""
"No longer emitting a `-Wpre-c2y-compat` or extension diagnostic about use of "
"octal literals with a `0o` prefix, and no longer emitting a `-Wdeprecated-"
"octal-literals` diagnostic for use of octal literals without a `0o` prefix, "
"when the literal is expanded from a macro defined in a system header. "
"(#GH192389)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:692
msgid ""
"Improved error recovery for missing semicolons after class members. Clang "
"now avoids skipping subsequent valid declarations when their previous decl "
"is missing semicolon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:695
msgid "Removed the body of lambdas from some diagnostic messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:697
msgid ""
"Fixed false positive host-device mismatch errors in discarded `if constexpr` "
"branches for CUDA/HIP; such calls are now correctly skipped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:700
msgid ""
"Clang now errors when a function declaration aliases a variable or vice "
"versa. (#GH195550)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:702
msgid ""
"Added `-Wattribute-alias` to diagnose type mismatches between an alias and "
"its aliased function. (#GH195550)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:704
msgid ""
"The diagnostics around `__block` now explain why a variable cannot be marked "
"`__block`. (#GH197213)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:706
msgid ""
"Extended `-Wnonportable-include-path` to warn about trailing whitespace and "
"dots in `#include` paths. (#GH190610)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:708
msgid ""
"Clang now emits error when attribute is missing closing `]]` followed by `;;"
"`. (#GH187223)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:710
msgid ""
"Clang now rejects inline asm constraints and clobbers that contain an "
"embedded null character, instead of silently truncating them. (#GH173900)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:713
msgid ""
"Diagnostics for the C++11 range-based for statement now report the correct "
"iterator type in notes for invalid iterator types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:716
msgid ""
"`-Wfortify-source` now warns when the constant-evaluated argument to `umask` "
"has bits set outside `0777`. Those bits are silently discarded by the "
"kernel, so setting them is almost always a typo (matching the bionic libc "
"`diagnose_if` check)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:721
msgid "Improved how Unicode characters are displayed in diagnostic messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:723
msgid ""
"`-Wtautological-pointer-compare` and `-Wpointer-bool-conversion` now "
"diagnose a reference to a function (e.g. of type `void (&)()`) compared "
"against or converted to a null pointer, the same as a bare function name. "
"(#GH46362)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:729
msgid "Improvements to Clang's time-trace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:731
msgid "Improvements to Coverage Mapping"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:733
msgid "[MC/DC] Nested expressions are handled as individual MC/DC expressions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:734
msgid ""
"\"Single byte coverage\" now supports branch coverage and can be used "
"together with `-fcoverage-mcdc`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:736
msgid ""
"Consteval member functions are no longer emitted in coverage mappings, "
"matching the existing behavior for free consteval functions. (#GH164448)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:739
msgid "Bug Fixes in This Version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:741
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion when comparing a fixed point type with a `_BitInt` type. "
"(#GH196948)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:742
msgid ""
"Fixed atomic boolean compound assignment; the conversion back to atomic bool "
"would be miscompiled. (#GH33210)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:743
msgid ""
"Correctly handle default template argument when establishing subsumption. "
"(#GH188640)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:744
msgid ""
"Fixed a failed assertion in the preprocessor when `__has_embed` parameters "
"are missing parentheses. (#GH175088)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:745
msgid ""
"Fix lifetime extension of temporaries in for-range-initializers in "
"templates. (#GH165182)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:746
msgid ""
"Fixed a preprocessor crash in `__has_cpp_attribute` on incomplete scoped "
"attributes. (#GH178098)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:747
msgid ""
"Fixes an assertion failure when evaluating `__underlying_type` on enum "
"redeclarations. (#GH177943)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:748
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion failure caused by nested macro expansion during header-"
"name lexing (`__has_embed(__has_include)`). (#GH178635)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:749
msgid ""
"Clang now outputs relative paths of embeds for dependency output. (#GH161950)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:750
msgid ""
"Fix the result type of a binary operation where both operands are 'void' l-"
"values. (#GH111300)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:751
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion failure when evaluating `_Countof` on invalid `void`-"
"typed operands. (#GH180893)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:752
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion failure in the serialized diagnostic printer when it is "
"destroyed without calling `finish()`. (#GH140433)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:753
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion failure caused by error recovery while extending a nested "
"name specifier with results from ordinary lookup. (#GH181470)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:754
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when parsing `#pragma clang attribute` arguments for "
"attributes that forbid arguments. (#GH182122)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:755
msgid ""
"Fixed a bug in how Clang re-transforms expressions produced from "
"substititions from type aliases and concept specializations. (#GH191738) "
"(#GH196375)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:757
msgid ""
"Fixed a bug with multiple-include optimization (MIOpt) state not being "
"preserved in some cases during lexing, which could suppress header-guard "
"mismatch diagnostics and interfere with include-guard optimization. "
"(#GH180155)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:758
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when normalizing constraints involving concept template "
"parameters whose index coincided with non-concept template parameters in the "
"same parameter mapping."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:759
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash caused by accessing dependent diagnostics of a non-dependent "
"context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:760
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when substituting into a non-type template parameter that has "
"a type containing an undeduced placeholder type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:761
msgid ""
"Fixed several crashes and improved diagnostics when a multidimensional "
"subscript operator is applied to a built-in type. (#GH187800)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:762
msgid ""
"Correctly diagnosing and no longer crashing when `export module foo` "
"(without a semicolon) are the final tokens in a module file. (#GH187771)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:764
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash in duplicate attribute checking caused by comparing constant "
"arguments with different integer signedness. (#GH188259)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:765
msgid ""
"Clang now emits an error when returning an initializer list from a lambda "
"with an explicit return type of void. The diagnostic now correctly refers to "
"\"lambda\" instead of \"block\". (#GH188661)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:768
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash on `_BitInt(N)` arrays where 129 ≤ N ≤ 192 due to incorrect "
"array filler lowering. (#GH189643)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:769
msgid ""
"Fixed the behavior in C23 of `auto`, by emitting an error when an array type "
"is specified for a `char *`. (#GH162694)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:770
msgid ""
"Fixed an issue where an assert was thrown instead of an error if no vulkan "
"env was specified with `--triple spirv`. (#GH189964)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:771
msgid ""
"Fixed incorrect rejection of `auto` with reordered declaration specifiers in "
"C23. (#GH164121)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:772
msgid ""
"Fixed a bug where Clang fails to find instantiation of Decls in constraint "
"checking. (#GH173086)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:773
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when assigning to an element of an `ext_vector_type` with "
"`bool` element type. (#GH189260)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:774
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash caused by declaring multiple `ownership_returns` attributes "
"with mismatched or missing arguments. (#GH188733)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:775
msgid ""
"Clang now emits an error for friend declarations of lambda members. "
"(#GH26540)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:776
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash caused by lambda capture handling in delayed default "
"arguments. (#GH176534)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:777
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when parsing invalid `static_assert` declarations with string-"
"literal messages (#GH187690)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:778
msgid ""
"Fixed a potential stack-use-after-return issue in Clang when copy-"
"initializing an array via an element-at-a-time copy loop (#GH192026)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:780
msgid ""
"Fixed an issue where certain designated initializers would be rejected for "
"constexpr variables. (#GH193373)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:781
msgid ""
"Fixed `clang::Preprocessor::recomputeCurLexerKind` to avoid default fallback "
"to `CurLexerCallback = CLK_CachingLexer;`. This prevents code-completion EOF "
"handling from accidentally restoring CLK_CachingLexer while a tentative "
"parse is still active, which could trigger a caching lexer re-entry "
"assertion in clangd signature help. (#GH200677)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:784
msgid "Fixed a crash when `#embed` is used with C++ modules (#GH195350)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:785
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion in constant evaluation when using a defaulted comparison "
"operator in a `union`. (#GH147127)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:786
msgid ""
"Fixed a bug where `-x cuda` caused clang to immediately resolve templates "
"that should not be. (#GH200545)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:787
msgid ""
"Fixed an issue where `__typeof_unqual` and `__typeof_unqual__` were rejected "
"as a declaration specifier in block scope in C++."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:788
msgid ""
"Fixed crash when checking for overflow for unary operator that can't "
"overflow (#GH170072)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:789
msgid ""
"Clang no longer handles a `\" q-char-sequence \"` header name as a string "
"literal (#GH132643)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:790
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion where we improperly handled implicit conversions to "
"integral types from an atomic-type with a conversion function. (#GH201770)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:791
msgid ""
"Fixed assertion failures involving code completion with delayed default "
"arguments and exception specifications. (#GH200879)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:792
msgid ""
"Fixed a regression where calling a function that takes a class-type "
"parameter by value inside `decltype` of a concept could be incorrectly "
"rejected when used as a non-type template argument. (#GH175831)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:793
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash in the constant evaluator when an ill-formed array new-"
"expression whose bound could not be determined (e.g. `new int[]()`) was used "
"in a constant expression. (#GH200139)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:795
msgid "Bug Fixes to Compiler Builtins"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:797
msgid ""
"Fix a crash when passing an unresolved overload set to "
"`__builtin_classify_type`. (#GH175589)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:798
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when calling `__builtin_allow_sanitize_check` with no "
"arguments. (#GH183927)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:799
msgid ""
"`__annotation` is now diagnosed as unsupported on non-Windows/UEFI targets, "
"fixing a crash when using it with `-fms-extensions` on other platforms. "
"(#GH184318)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:801
msgid ""
"Fixed a compiler crash due to an unresolved overloaded function type when "
"calling `__builtin_bit_cast`. (#GH200112)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:803
msgid ""
"Clang now SFINAE friendly when the ``__reference_meows_from_temporary`` "
"builtins should SFINAE friendly when the 1st type is not a reference type. "
"(#GH206524)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:805
msgid ""
"Fixed `__builtin_offsetof` incorrectly sign-extending unsigned array indices "
"with the high bit set (e.g. `uint8_t` values >= 128), which produced wrong "
"offset values in constant expressions. (#GH199319)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:810
msgid "Bug Fixes to Attribute Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:812
msgid ""
"Fixed a behavioral discrepancy between deleted functions and private members "
"when checking the `enable_if` attribute. (#GH175895)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:813
msgid ""
"Fixed `init_priority` attribute by delaying type checks until after the type "
"is deduced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:814
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when a `section` attribute or `#pragma clang section` caused a "
"section type conflict with a declaration whose name is not a simple "
"identifier, such as a lambda's call operator. (#GH192264)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:817
msgid ""
"Fixed a regression where attributed types (such as those carrying `_Nonnull`/"
"`_Nullable` attributes) were not deduplicated, because the attributes' "
"arguments were not taken into account when uniquing them. The duplications "
"could substantially increase the size of precompiled headers and modules "
"(PCH/PCM), and the time spent loading them. (#GH200961)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:823
msgid "Bug Fixes to C++ Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:825
msgid ""
"Fixed a preprocessor assertion failure triggered when parsing an invalid "
"template-id starting with `::template operator`. (#GH186582)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:826
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when a function template is defined as a non-template friend "
"with a global scope qualifier. (#GH185341)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:827
msgid ""
"Clang now rejects constant template parameters with block pointer types, "
"since these are not implemented anyway and would lead to crashes. (#GH189247)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:828
msgid ""
"Clang no longer reject call expressions whose type is a not-yet-deduced auto "
"type. (#GH207565)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:829
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash on error recovery when dealing with invalid templates. "
"(#GH183075)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:830
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when instantiating `requires` expressions involving "
"substitution failures in C++ concepts. (#GH176402)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:831
msgid ""
"Concepts appearing in the require-clause of a member function no longer have "
"access to non-public members of that class, or to a current class object. "
"(#GH115838) (#GH194803) (#GH197067)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:833
msgid "We no longer caches invalid variable specializations. (#GH132592)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:834
msgid ""
"Fixed an incorrect template argument deduction when matching packs of "
"template template parameters when one of its parameters is also a pack. "
"(#GH181166)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:836
msgid ""
"Clang no longer errors on overloads with different ref-qualifiers and "
"constraints. (#GH120812)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:837
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when a default argument is passed to an explicit object "
"parameter. (#GH176639)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:838
msgid "Fixed an alias template CTAD crash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:839
msgid ""
"Correctly diagnose uses of `co_await` / `co_yield` in the default argument "
"of nested function declarations. (#GH98923)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:840
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when diagnosing an invalid static member function with an "
"explicit object parameter (#GH177741)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:841
msgid ""
"Clang incorrectly instantiated variable specializations outside of the "
"immediate context. (#GH54439)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:842
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when pack expansions are used as arguments for non-pack "
"parameters of built-in templates. (#GH180307)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:843
msgid "Fixed crash instantiating class member specializations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:844
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash during class template instantiation when a member variable "
"template's type substitution fails (e.g. `typename T::type` with `T=int`), "
"which left the `VarTemplateDecl` unregistered and caused a subsequent "
"assertion failure when instantiating a partial specialization of that "
"member. (#GH198890)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:849
msgid ""
"Fix a problem where a substitution failure when evaluating a type "
"requirement could directly make the program ill-formed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:851
msgid ""
"Typo correction now corrects the name qualifier for invalid template names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:852
msgid ""
"Fix a problem where pack index expressions where incorrectly being regarded "
"as equivalent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:853
msgid "Correctly diagnose narrowing in pack index expressions. (#GH205650)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:854
msgid ""
"Fixed a bug where captured variables in non-mutable lambdas were incorrectly "
"treated as mutable when used inside decltype in the return type. (#GH180460)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:856
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when evaluating uninitialized GCC vector/ext_vector_type "
"vectors in `constexpr`. (#GH180044)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:857
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when `explicit(bool)` is used with an incomplete enumeration. "
"(#GH183887)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:858
msgid ""
"Fix crash-on-invalid caused by qualified forward declarations. (#GH202320)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:859
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash on `typeid` of incomplete local types during template "
"instantiation. (#GH63242), (#GH176397)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:860
msgid ""
"Fixed spurious diagnostics produced when checking if constraints are "
"equivalent for redeclarations, which could make the program mistakenly ill-"
"formed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:862
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when an immediate-invoked `consteval` lambda is used as an "
"invalid initializer. (#GH185270)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:863
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion failure when using a global destructor with a target with "
"a non-default program address space. (#GH186484)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:864
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when instantiating an invalid out-of-line static data member "
"definition in a local class. (#GH176152)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:865
msgid ""
"Inherited constructors in `dllexport` classes are now exported for ABI-"
"compatible cases, matching MSVC behavior. Constructors with variadic "
"arguments or callee-cleanup parameters are not yet supported and produce a "
"warning. (#GH162640)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:868
msgid ""
"Correctly diagnose invalid non-dependent calls in dependent contexts. "
"(#GH135694)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:869
msgid ""
"Fix initialization of GRO when GRO-return type mismatches, as part of "
"CWG2563. (#GH98744)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:870
msgid ""
"Fix an error using an initializer list with array new for a type that is not "
"default-constructible. (#GH81157)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:871
msgid ""
"We no longer consider conversion operators when copy-initializing from the "
"same type. This was non conforming and could lead to recursive constraint "
"satisfaction checking. (#GH149443)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:873
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash in Itanium C++ name mangling for a lambda in a local class "
"field initializer inside a constructor/destructor. (#GH176395)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:874
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when Expr::ClassifyImpl computes a classification like "
"CL_LValue or CL_PRValue, then asserts that this agrees with the AST node's "
"own value category. (#GH202693)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:876
msgid ""
"Fixed crashes in Itanium C++ name mangling for lambdas with trailing "
"requires-clauses involving requires-expressions. (#GH100774) (#GH123854)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:877
msgid ""
"Fixed an invalid rejection and assertion failure while generating "
"`operator=` for fields with the `__restrict` qualifier. (#GH37979)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:878
msgid ""
"Fixed a use-after-free bug when parsing default arguments containing lambdas "
"in declarations with template-id declarators. (#GH196725)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:879
msgid ""
"Fixed missing destructor cleanups for lambda init-captures in default member "
"initializers used during aggregate initialization. (#GH196469)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:881
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash in constant evaluation using placement new on an array which "
"was later initialized. (#GH196450)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:882
msgid ""
"Fixed an issue where Clang incorrectly accepted invalid unqualified uses of "
"local nested class names outside their declaring scope. (#GH184622)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:883
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when parsing invalid friend declaration with storage-class "
"specifier. (#GH186569)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:884
msgid ""
"Fixed a missing vtable for `dynamic_cast<FinalClass *>(this)` in a function "
"template. (#GH198511)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:885
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion failure during init-list checking of an array whose "
"element type is an incomplete class. (#GH140685)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:886
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when using a pack indexing type (e.g. ``Ts...[0]``) imported "
"from another module. (#GH204479)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:887
msgid ""
"Fixed an ODR-merging error in modules, where class-scope `using enum` "
