msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1071
msgid ""
"Add support for `#pragma export` for z/OS. This is a pragma used to export "
"functions and variables with external linkage from shared libraries. It "
"provides compatibility with the IBM XL C/C++ compiler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1075
msgid "DWARF Support in Clang"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1077
msgid "Floating Point Support in Clang"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1079
msgid "Fixed Point Support in Clang"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1081
msgid "AST Matchers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1083
msgid ""
"Fixed `nullPointerConstant` matcher falsely matching integer literal `0` in "
"non-null-pointer contexts such as array subscripts and pointer arithmetic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1085
msgid "Add `functionTypeLoc` matcher for matching `FunctionTypeLoc`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1086
msgid ""
"Add missing support for `TraversalKind` in some `addMatcher()` overloads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1088
msgid "clang-format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1090
msgid ""
"Add `ObjCSpaceAfterMethodDeclarationPrefix` option to control space between "
"the '-'/'+' and the return type in Objective-C method declarations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1092
msgid ""
"Deprecate the `BinPackParameters` and `BinPackArguments` options and replace "
"them with the `PackParameters` and `PackArguments` structs (respectively) to "
"unify packing behavior. Add the `BreakAfter` option to the structs, allowing "
"parameter and argument lists to be formatted with one parameter/argument on "
"each line if they exceed the specified count."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1097
msgid ""
"Add `AfterComma` value to `BreakConstructorInitializers` to allow breaking "
"constructor initializers after commas, keeping the colon on the same line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1099
msgid ""
"Extend `BreakBinaryOperations` to accept a structured configuration with per-"
"operator break rules and minimum chain length gating via `PerOperator`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1101
msgid ""
"Add `AllowShortRecordOnASingleLine` option and set it to `EmptyAndAttached` "
"for LLVM style."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1102
msgid ""
"Add `BreakFunctionDeclarationParameters` option to always break before "
"function declaration parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1104
msgid ""
"Add `EnumAssignments` option to `AlignConsecutiveAssignments` for aligning "
"enum assignments without affecting other assignments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1106
msgid ""
"Add `BreakBeforeReturnType` option to break before the function return type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1109
msgid "libclang"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1111
msgid ""
"Visit constraints of `auto` type to properly visit concept usages (#GH166580)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1112
msgid ""
"Visit switch initializer statements (<https://bugs.kde.org/show_bug.cgi?"
"id=415537#c2>)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1113
msgid ""
"Fix crash in clang_getBinaryOperatorKindSpelling and "
"clang_getUnaryOperatorKindSpelling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1114
msgid ""
"The clang_Module_getASTFile API is deprecated and now always returns nullptr"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1115
msgid ""
"The clang_Cursor_getCommentRange API will now return a comment range for "
"macro definitions that have documentation comments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1116
msgid ""
"Added CXType_PredefinedSugar for `__ptrdiff_t`, `__size_t`, and "
"`__signed_size_t` types, which are no longer exposed as CXType_Unexposed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1120
msgid "Code Completion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1122
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash in code completion when using a C-Style cast with a "
"parenthesized operand in Objective-C++ mode. (#GH180125)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1124
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when code completion is triggered inside an ill-formed "
"lambda's trailing requires-clause. (#GH201632)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1126
msgid "Static Analyzer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1128
msgid ""
"The `-analyzer-constraints` option `z3` was renamed to `unsupported-z3` "
"because the Z3-based (constraint) solver was known for crashing for years "
"now. Didn't receive support, so it was marked unsupported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1132
msgid "Crash and bug fixes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1134
msgid ""
"Fixed `security.VAList` checker producing false positives when analyzing C23 "
"code where `va_start` expands to `__builtin_c23_va_start`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1136
msgid ""
"Fixed a compiler crash when combining `_Atomic` and `__auto_type` in C, for "
"example `_Atomic __auto_type x = expr`. (#GH118058)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1139 ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1234
msgid "Improvements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1141
msgid ""
"`alpha.unix.PthreadLock` now emits path notes on lock, unlock, destroy, and "
"init operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1152
msgid "Moved checkers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1154
msgid "The checker `unix.cstring.UninitializedRead` is now out of alpha."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1158
msgid "Sanitizers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1160
msgid "UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer now supports `__ubsan_default_suppressions`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1161
msgid ""
"Sanitizer Special Case Lists (`-fsanitize-ignorelist`) now support Version 4 "
"of the Special Case List format, which introduces a transition period for "
"leading dot-slash (`./`) canonicalization in path matching. Version 4 "
"matches both canonicalized and non-canonicalized paths but emits a warning "
"for deprecated matches. Version 5 drops backward compatibility and requires "
"rules to match canonicalized paths (without leading `./`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1167
msgid ""
"Sanitizer Special Case Lists (`-fsanitize-ignorelist`) and warning "
"suppression mappings (`--warning-suppression-mappings`) now recognize "
"version 4 of the Special Case List format (indicated by `#!special-case-list-"
"v4`). On Windows hosts, path matching is slash-agnostic (both forward "
"slashes (`/`) and backslashes (`\\`) match either path separator in both "
"patterns and paths)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1173
msgid "Python Binding Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1175
msgid ""
"Add deprecation warnings to `CompletionChunk.isKind...` methods. These will "
"be removed in a future release. Existing uses should be adapted to directly "
"compare equality of the `CompletionChunk` kind with the corresponding "
"`CompletionChunkKind` variant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1180
msgid ""
"Affected methods: `isKindOptional`, `isKindTypedText`, `isKindPlaceHolder`, "
"`isKindInformative` and `isKindResultType`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1183
msgid ""
"Add a deprecation warning to `CodeCompletionResults.results`. This property "
"will become an implementation detail with changed behavior in a future "
"release and should not be used directly.. Existing uses of "
"`CodeCompletionResults.results` should be changed to directly use "
"`CodeCompletionResults`: it nows supports `__len__` and `__getitem__`, so it "
"can be used the same as `CodeCompletionResults.results`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1190
msgid ""
"Added a new helper method `get_clang_version` to the class `Config` to read "
"the version string of the libclang in use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1193
msgid "OpenMP Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1195
msgid "Added support for `transparent` clause in task and taskloop directives."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1196
msgid ""
"Added support for `use_device_ptr` clause to accept an optional `fallback` "
"modifier (`fb_nullify` or `fb_preserve`) with OpenMP >= 61."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1198
msgid ""
"Added support for `local` clause with declare_target directive when OpenMP "
">= 60."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1200
msgid ""
"Fixed the identity element used for `reduction(* : x)` over C++ class types "
"(e.g. `std::complex`). The private copy is now initialized to the "
"multiplicative identity instead of being value-initialized, which previously "
"produced a wrong result (the product collapsed to the additive identity)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1205
msgid "SYCL Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1207
msgid ""
"SYCL compilations now default to `-std=c++17` when no explicit language "
"standard is specified. Standards below C++17 are rejected with a diagnostic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1209
msgid ""
"Clang now assumes default target for SYCL device compilation is 64-bit SPIR-"
"V and it now diagnoses if a non-supporting target is specified via command "
"line. (#GH167358)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1212
msgid ""
"The SYCL runtime shared library has been renamed from `libsycl.so` to "
"`libLLVMSYCL.so` to align with LLVM naming conventions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1214
msgid ""
"SYCL header include paths are now added automatically for both host and "
"device compilations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1216
msgid ""
"SYCL runtime library linking is now supported on Windows. When `-fsycl` is "
"specified, Clang automatically adds `/MD` if no explicit CRT flag is "
"present, links the appropriate debug (`LLVMSYCLd.lib`) or release (`LLVMSYCL."
"lib`) library, and rejects static CRT flags (`/MT`, `/MTd`) with a "
"diagnostic. Use `-nolibsycl` to suppress automatic library linking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1222
msgid ""
"Fixed `-nolibsycl` being silently ignored on Linux: the SYCL runtime library "
"was unconditionally added to the link line even when the flag was passed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1225
msgid ""
"Added the `-fsycl-device-image-split=` option to select the granularity at "
"which SYCL device code is grouped into device images. Supported values are "
"`kernel` (one device image per kernel), `translation_unit` (one device image "
"per translation unit), and `link_unit` (one device image per linking unit). "
"The bare `-fsycl-device-image-split` flag is an alias for `-fsycl-device-"
"image-split=translation_unit`, which is also the default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1231
msgid ""
"Clang now is capable of diagnosing reference kernel parameters which are not "
"allowed by SYCL 2020 spec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1236
msgid "Improved substitution performance in concept checking. (#GH172266)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:1237
msgid ""
"Clang now preserves the left-hand side of a binary expression (such as an "
"assignment or comparison) in a `RecoveryExpr` when the right-hand side fails "
"to parse. This improves IDE features like go-to-definition in `clangd`."
msgstr ""

